# ---- 2026-10-16: shared study with icefall, agreed lists ----
# GRID test = all 4,000 clips (24,000 words); Lombard = shared clip set, eval-40
# speakers (plain = plain-speech clips, eval-40). LM weight chosen on the 14
# Lombard dev speakers. Base, layer 10 through the e2e chain (+CMVN), chain
# seed 0; three encoder fine-tunes per arm (common.seed 1337, 43, 44).
# arm               seed  valid  GRID  Lombard  plain
# LoRA r32          1337  5.10   6.34  5.70     5.95   input/avhubert_base_ctc_lora.pt
# LoRA r32            43  4.83   6.44  6.06     6.03   input/avhubert_base_ctc_lora_s43.pt
# LoRA r32            44  5.02   6.19  5.94     6.52   input/avhubert_base_ctc_lora_s44.pt
#   mean                         6.32  5.90     6.17
# full fine-tune    1337  5.48   5.70  7.68     8.88   input/avhubert_base_ctc_full.pt
# full fine-tune      43  5.40   6.74  7.87     8.43   input/avhubert_base_ctc_full_s43.pt
# full fine-tune      44  5.21   6.08  7.38     7.89   input/avhubert_base_ctc_full_s44.pt
#   mean                         6.17  7.64     8.40
# full, lr 5e-5     1337  5.23   6.41  6.58      -     input/avhubert_base_ctc_full_lr5e-5.pt
# full, lr 5e-4     1337  7.92   7.43  11.81     -     input/avhubert_base_ctc_full_lr5e-4.pt
# full, AdamW 0.01  1337  5.58   6.60  8.34     8.99   input/avhubert_base_ctc_full_wd1e-2.pt
# The older lines above use the 3,985-clip test (23,910 words) and the
# 2,577-clip all-54 Lombard set (15,462 words) with test-chosen LM weights.
